  "slug": "lunar-chest",
  "note": "Lunar Chest's real mechanic lives in ==Loot mechanics== prose, not in its drop rows. Each Moon killed before opening gives an INDEPENDENT 1/56 at a piece of that Moon's own 4-item set; if it hits, the piece is drawn uniformly from that set's not-yet-obtained pieces (duplicate protection scoped per set, not across all 12 uniques). Any unique hit suppresses the standard table entirely; otherwise standard loot rolls 1x/3x/6x for 1/2/3 Moons. The parser saw only a flat 12-entry weighted table at denominator 224 \u2014 the page states that 1/224 figure is the naive first-piece-only rate that does NOT account for duplicate protection, so it is not used as a rate anywhere here. Known modelling assumption, flagged rather than hidden: a 1/56 trigger for a set the player has already completed still counts as a hit for suppression purposes, since the engine decides suppression at the access roll; the page says such a roll does 'nothing useful' but does not say whether it still blocks standard loot. Affects only players holding a full set. Source: Lunar Chest, revid 15284737.",
